---
// Visual "required" marker for a label. It is an aria-hidden SVG rather than a literal "*" so the
// field's accessible name stays just the label text; the input's `required` attribute is what
// assistive tech announces. The no-break space is the gap (a margin would still let the mark wrap
// onto a line of its own), so the mark always travels with the label's last word.
---

<!-- prettier-ignore -->
<span aria-hidden="true">&nbsp;<svg
    viewBox="0 0 8 8"
    class="inline-block size-[0.4rem] align-[0.4em]"
    fill="none"
    stroke="currentColor"
    stroke-width="1.2"
    stroke-linecap="round"
  >
    <path d="M4 .5v7M.97 2.25l6.06 3.5M.97 5.75l6.06-3.5"></path>
  </svg>
</span>
